<section class="page" id="where"><h2 class="page-title">WHERE IT IS</h2><div class="sub">An island at the tip of India</div>
<div class="g2" style="align-items:start">
<div><svg class="pg-fig" width="300" height="320" viewBox="0 0 300 320" role="img" aria-label="Simplified map of India with Rameswaram marked on the south-east coast of Tamil Nadu, facing Sri Lanka"><rect width="300" height="320" fill="#eef3fa"/><path d="M120 20 L150 14 L170 34 L160 60 L190 80 L230 84 L262 104 L280 100 L290 120 L260 130 L250 150 L226 160 L200 190 L176 240 L160 290 L150 300 L140 288 L120 230 L100 200 L72 180 L50 170 L40 150 L60 140 L54 120 L80 100 L96 80 L110 50Z" fill="#dfeccf" stroke="#111" stroke-width="2"/><ellipse cx="190" cy="300" rx="14" ry="18" fill="#dfeccf" stroke="#111" stroke-width="2"/><text x="214" y="312" font-family="Bangers" font-size="9" fill="#555">Sri Lanka</text><circle cx="170" cy="276" r="7" fill="#e63946" stroke="#111" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M178 272 L220 250" stroke="#c0392b" stroke-width="2"/><text x="244" y="246" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Bangers" font-size="12" fill="#c0392b">RĀMEŚVARAM</text><circle cx="196" cy="118" r="4" fill="#111"/><text x="196" y="110" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Bangers" font-size="10" fill="#111">Kāśī</text><path d="M196 122 C 200 180, 190 230, 172 270" fill="none" stroke="#c0392b" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="4 4"/><text x="150" y="312" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Bangers" font-size="10" fill="#555">India (simplified outline)</text></svg></div>
<div class="panel reading">
<p>Rāmeśvaram stands on <b>Pāmban island</b>, off the south-east coast of Tamil Nadu, joined to the mainland at Maṇḍapam by the <b>Pāmban</b> road and rail bridges.</p>
<p>The island points east toward Sri Lanka. At its tip, <b>Dhanuṣkoḍi</b>, a chain of sandbanks and shoals, <b>Rāma Setu</b> (Adam's Bridge), runs toward Mannar island across the shallow sea.</p>
<p>To the north lies Palk Bay; to the south, the <b>Gulf of Mannar</b>, a marine national park of coral reefs.</p>
</div>
</div>
<svg class="pg-fig" width="560" height="320" viewBox="0 0 560 320" role="img" aria-label="Simple map of Pamban island showing the Pamban bridges from Mandapam, Pamban town, the Ramanathaswamy temple and Agni Tirtham in Rameswaram town, Gandhamadana Parvatam, Kalam memorial, the road to Dhanushkodi and Arichal Munai, and Rama Setu toward Sri Lanka"><rect width="560" height="320" fill="#4aa3df"/><path d="M0 120 h40 v60 h-40z" fill="#dfeccf" stroke="#111" stroke-width="2"/><text x="20" y="200" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Bangers" font-size="10" fill="#111">Maṇḍapam</text><path d="M40 146 h70" stroke="#111" stroke-width="5"/><path d="M40 156 h70" stroke="#888" stroke-width="4"/><text x="76" y="138" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Bangers" font-size="10" fill="#fff">PĀMBAN BRIDGES</text><path d="M110 120 C 160 100, 240 90, 300 100 C 340 108, 360 130, 380 160 C 400 190, 450 220, 500 250 L 510 262 C 470 250, 420 230, 380 214 C 340 200, 300 200, 250 196 C 190 192, 140 190, 110 180Z" fill="#dfeccf" stroke="#111" stroke-width="2.5"/><text x="140" y="172" font-family="Bangers" font-size="10" fill="#111">Pāmban</text><g transform="translate(300 150) scale(0.45)"><rect x="-30" y="-30" width="60" height="30" fill="#f2e6d0" stroke="#111" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M-20 -30 L-16 -100 L16 -100 L20 -30Z" fill="#f2e6d0" stroke="#111" stroke-width="2.5"/><path d="M-16 -100 q16 -12 32 0z" fill="#e0a800" stroke="#111" stroke-width="2"/></g><text x="300" y="170" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Bangers" font-size="12" fill="#c0392b">RĀMANĀTHASVĀMĪ</text><circle cx="330" cy="126" r="6" fill="#ffd60a" stroke="#111"/><text x="340" y="122" font-family="Bangers" font-size="10" fill="#111">Agni Tīrtham</text><circle cx="270" cy="112" r="5" fill="#7a3fa0" stroke="#111"/><text x="262" y="100" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Bangers" font-size="9" fill="#111">Gandhamādana</text><circle cx="200" cy="182" r="5" fill="#2a9d6f" stroke="#111"/><text x="200" y="200" text-anchor="middle" font-