<section class="page" id="end">
  <h2 class="page-title">RĀMEŚVARAM ON ONE PAGE</h2>
  <div class="sub">Rāma's Lord at the southern sea, in five lines</div>
  <div class="steps">
    <div><b>The jyotirliṅga.</b> Rāmanātha at Rāmeśvaram: seventh of the twelve, the southern Cār Dhām, the liṅga Rāma worshipped.</div>
    <div><b>The legends.</b> Sītā's sand liṅga and Hanumān's Viśvaliṅga, worshipped first; the bridge, Dhanuṣkoḍi and Vibhīṣaṇa.</div>
    <div><b>The history.</b> Tevāram hymns; Parākramabāhu's sanctum; Pāṇḍyas and Jaffna kings; the Setupatis' corridors (to 1772); the 1964 cyclone; the 2025 bridge.</div>
    <div><b>The rituals.</b> Agni Tīrtham and the 22 wells; the dawn crystal liṅga; rites for ancestors on the shore.</div>
    <div><b>The bond.</b> Kāśī to Rāmeśvaram: sand to the Gaṅgā, Gaṅgā to Rāmanātha.</div>
  </div>
