  <div class="panel reading small">
    <p><b>Temple:</b> Wikipedia's "Ramanathaswamy Temple" and sources it cites (Parākramabāhu I, 1153–86; 11th–12th-century vimānas; Kiḻavan Setupati; corridors totalling about 3,850 ft and about 1,212 pillars; 22 tīrthas as Rāma's arrows; Setupati gifts 1745–1837); Business Today (September 2026), citing the Rāmanāthapuram district website, for the outer corridor's 197 m × 133 m.</p>
    <p><b>Corridors:</b> Tamil Nadu tourism sources on the third corridor (begun 1722, completed 1772 under Muttu Rāmaliṅga Setupati); the 53 m rājagopuram.</p>
    <p><b>Bridges and cyclone:</b> Deccan Herald, The South First, Swarajya, Lokmat Times and All India Radio (new Pāmban bridge, 6 April 2025; 1914 bridge; 1964 cyclone; road bridge 1988).</p>
    <p><b>Legends:</b> traditional accounts from later Rāmāyaṇas and the Setu Māhātmya of the Skanda Purāṇa, retold briefly; versions differ.</p>
    <p><b>Not independently verified:</b> the origin of the crystal liṅga; the names and order of daily pūjās; festival months; the Jaffna kings' "Setukāvalan" title; Vivekananda's landing date; the wording of the long stotram's seventh verse; the length of Rāma Setu (given as approximate).</p>
